* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    call !acc_os_place(acc.name, staged.path, target.path, err)
*
* A per-OS helper of RESTORE.ACCOUNT (see !acc_archive).  target.path is the
* account's register path.  In Solo the one account, sduser, always exists
* (solo_account makes it at install), and it is the account every session is
* in, so the swap cannot run inside a session.  PLANNED, NOT BUILT OR AGREED:
* SD's start-up would call this before any session opens (owner, 1 Oct 2026:
* a backup restored onto another Solo replaces that Solo's data).
*
* THE TARGET DIRECTORY STAYS AND ITS CONTENTS ARE SWAPPED, as in the
* multi-user product, so the directory keeps whatever ACL it has.  The old
* contents are moved aside first and removed only once all of the new ones are
* in; a failure before that puts everything back.  Then every child is reset to
* inherit the target's ACL, because a moved file keeps the one it had.  Both
* trees must hold a voc, so a wrong path cannot empty some other directory.
* The work is sd-account-archive.ps1 -Mode Place.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine acc_os_place(acc.name, staged.path, target.path, err)
$catalog !acc_os_place

   counts = ''
   call !acc_archive('PLACE', '', staged.path : @fm : target.path, counts, err)
   return
end
